From: OpenWrt developers <openwrt-devel@lists.openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: omit nwfilter when network management is disabled

OpenWrt owns its firewall. In a build without the network driver,
firewall_backend_priority is unset, so enabling nwfilter unconditionally
also breaks Meson configuration.

---
diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -2031,7 +2031,7 @@
 
 # nwfilter should only be compiled for linux, and only if the
 # libvirt daemon is also being compiled
-if conf.has('WITH_LIBVIRTD') and host_machine.system() == 'linux'
+if conf.has('WITH_LIBVIRTD') and conf.has('WITH_NETWORK') and host_machine.system() == 'linux'
   conf.set('WITH_NWFILTER', 1)
 endif
 
